Source: secubox-antirootkit
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Gérald Kerma <devel@cybermind.fr>
Build-Depends: debhelper (>= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2

Package: secubox-antirootkit
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, auditd, debsums, python3, python3-fastapi | python3-pip
Recommends: aide, rkhunter, chkrootkit
Description: SecuBox Anti-Rootkit - host-IDS anti-escape + exec scanner
 Host-based intrusion detection: an auditd-fed exec-surveillance scanner
 that jails unknown/non-dpkg-backed executables into an egress-blocked
 cgroup (anti-escape), an integrity wrap around debsums/aide/rkhunter/
 chkrootkit, and an alert-only manual quarantine workflow (never
 auto-deletes or auto-chmods a suspect binary — it only emits an
 operator-reviewable plan).
 .
 Targeted auditd watches (low volume by design) cover the common unbacked
 exec surface: /usr/local/bin, /usr/local/sbin, /tmp, /dev/shm, /opt and
 /usr/lib/jvm.
